---
---

<section id="demo" class="py-20 md:py-32 bg-gray-50">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
    <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-center fade-in">
      Same campaign. Read both.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-center text-gray-400 mt-4 text-lg fade-in">These came from the same prompt.</p>

    <div class="mt-16 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
      <!-- Recipient A -->
      <div class="border border-gray-200 bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 fade-in-left">
        <div class="mb-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Recipient</p>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold mt-1">John</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Interests</p>
          <div class="flex gap-2 mt-2">
            <span class="text-sm border border-gray-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1">AI</span>
            <span class="text-sm border border-gray-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1">Startups</span>
            <span class="text-sm border border-gray-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1">YC</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Generated email</p>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-5 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border border-gray-100">
            <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 mb-2">John —</p>
            <p>Quick one. We built a tool that rewrites your campaign for each person on your list. Figured it'd click for you since you're deep in the AI/startup world and probably tired of sending the same Mailchimp blast to everyone.</p>
            <p class="mt-2">Open to a quick look?</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Recipient B -->
      <div class="border border-gray-900 bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 fade-in-right">
        <div class="mb-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Recipient</p>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold mt-1">Sarah</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Interests</p>
          <div class="flex gap-2 mt-2">
            <span class="text-sm border border-gray-900 rounded-full px-3 py-1">Fitness</span>
            <span class="text-sm border border-gray-900 rounded-full px-3 py-1">Nutrition</span>
            <span class="text-sm border border-gray-900 rounded-full px-3 py-1">Wellness</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Generated email</p>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-5 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border border-gray-100">
            <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 mb-2">Hey Sarah,</p>
            <p>You know how most marketing emails from wellness brands feel super generic? We made something that fixes that. ulak takes your one campaign and rewrites it for each subscriber — so someone into marathon training gets a totally different email than someone focused on meal prep.</p>
            <p class="mt-2">Two-minute demo if you're curious.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
